notes={
366544:('parked_infinite_uniformity_gap','primary_definition_and_conjecture_body_plus_exact_search','Conjecture 4; definitions before Conjecture 1 and Tables 2–4','Exact Euler pentagonal recurrence computes p(n) for n <= 10000. Integer binary-search roots check k = 2..32 and retain every distance <= 10. No finite search establishes stabilization: the required assertion is uniform in unbounded n after k exceeds N_d.','Prove a uniform exclusion of p(n) within d of nontrivial kth powers for all sufficiently large k. Finite n cannot disprove eventual stabilization; a witness sequence with k unbounded would be needed.'),
366685:('parked_supplement_validation_gap','primary_definition_proposition_and_extended_diagnostic','Equation (1.2), Conjecture 6.8, Proposition 6.9; author-linked generatingfunctions.txt','Evaluated all supplied h_d/(1-t)^d for 4 <= d <= 30 and 2 <= n <= 50000 with exact finite differences, screening cross-d equality. No collisions. For high d this exceeds the source verification value ceiling 10^23. BUT supplied h30 gives a different p30(666) from the printed example; counts are conditional on this input file. n=1 trivial equalities are discarded as endpoint corrections.','Reconcile the author coefficient file against a trustworthy independent enumeration. Then pursue integral points beyond this bounded window; no global injectivity argument obtained.'),
366709:('parked_source_already_covers_small_range','primary_necessary_condition_proof_and_exact_polynomial_search','Theorems 1.4 and 1.6, Corollary 1.7, Proposition 4.1','Exact rational evaluation of Phi_s checks 2 <= s <= 15, 2 <= r <= 150 for all s distinct integral roots in [1,r+s-1]; none. The source already proves the classification for n <= 4000000, so this is replication only. Its necessary condition forces s >= 5000r(14.5+log r)^2 in any remaining case.','Remove the high-degree, r small regime in the integer-zero classification and bridge to existence/nonexistence of actual codes. No code search outside the source range completed.'),
366891:('parked_bounded_identity_checks','primary_profile_definition_and_conjecture_plus_exact_coefficients','Definition 2.1, introductory CP definition, Conjecture 7.1','Enumerated pairs of partitions with at most n parts directly, checked profile inequalities, and compared coefficients with both Gaussian-binomial expressions for k = 4..12, all 1 <= i <= k, n = 1..7, through q^18. All 1008 parameter cases match. No universal identity inferred.','Prove the finite-height two-row cylindric generating function for arbitrary profile; low q degree cannot address all sizes.'),
367011:('parked_realization_count_backend_gap','primary_extension_definition_tables_and_conjecture','Section 8, Figure 12 discussion, Tables 38–39, Conjecture 4','Recovered that 511 means K5 minus an edge in the five old neighbours, and X/V describes the two deleted edges. Text calls the step a 1-extension despite describing the deletion of two edges and insertion of a degree-five vertex. Source scope takes precedence; no typo counterexample pursued. No exact complex realization-count sweep completed.','Need a certified generic complex realization solver beyond nine vertices or a fibre-degree argument for the replacement, including all placements of deleted edges. Numerical geometric specializations alone do not certify the generic count.'),
367110:('excluded_author_reported_refutation','original_conjecture_and_current_primary_comparison_read','v1 Section 7, Conjecture 7.5; current Remark 7.10 and Theorem 7.6','The original Samokhin–van der Kallen comparison is replaced in the current source by a different collection. Remark 7.10 explicitly reports a Type A4 counterexample to the old comparison, after agreement in A2,B2,G2,A3,B3. The current theorem for their replacement collection is not a proof of the old conjecture.','No new route: author-reported prior counterexample. Its actual Sage/Mathematica witness was not independently reconstructed here; do not claim a new proof or Lean result.'),
367279:('parked_higher_relation_complex_gap','primary_definition_theorem_proof_and_conjecture_read','Theorem 1.9 proof, Proposition 8.2, Conjecture 8.3','Source line-closure proof gives ordinary formality from coordinate forms. It does not supply higher k-formality. Rank <= 4 and free cases are already settled in the source. No higher-relation-chain-complex implementation completed, so no claimed graph enumeration coverage.','Implement Brandt–Terao higher relation spaces with certified localization maps in rank >= 5; ordinary nullspace generation is insufficient.'),
367560:('excluded_source_reports_published_resolution','primary_conjecture_context_and_adjacent_theorem_statements_read','Conjecture 1.2 and paragraph following; Theorem 1.6; references Xu–Li–Zhou and Ota–Sanka','The literal MathDB record and primary source already say the conjecture was independently confirmed. References are Discrete Math. 347 (2024), 113755 and 113841. The source theorem has toughness > 1 and Hamiltonian-connected conclusion, so it must not be substituted for the stated toughness >= 1 theorem.','Published exact-resolution bodies were not separately retrieved; this is source-reported resolution, not independently re-proved. No redundant small-graph sweep performed.'),
367758:('parked_sustained_exact_and_structured_search','primary_definition_proofs_original_data_and_published_text_read','Definition 2.1, Lemma 2.1; v2 Table 1 and Conjecture 5.1; current Conjecture 4.2','All noncrossing layer orderings enumerated through 18 stamps, with every MV assignment counted and all maximizing assignments classified. n=18: 184940388 total layer orders, maximum 6530; no structural violation. Exact targeted assignment counts at n=22,26,30 use one-bit hill-climbing and test illegal neighbouring runs, beyond the source full enumeration through 21. These do not certify a global maximum.','Need a global comparison/injection excluding a run >= 4 or adjacent runs 3,3, or exhaustive generation of all assignments beyond 21. Source upper bounds are too loose; a locally superior illegal assignment would still require excluding all allowed assignments.'),
367836:('parked_source_cost_exceeds_lane_cap','primary_exact_conjecture_and_computational_method_read','Conjecture 8, Theorem 9, Appendix C.1','Source verifies the exact plane Hamiltonian subdrawing conjecture through n=9, requiring about 3 CPU days. Its n=10 verification concerns other conjectures, not this 2n-3-edge strengthening. No arbitrary-topological-drawing enumeration was run. Convex drawings are source-proved and cannot yield a counterexample.','Need faithful pre-rotation-system realizability and crossing constraints, then an n >= 10 SAT search. This is not interchangeable with straight-line random point sampling and was not completed under per-call caps.'),
367848:('excluded_source_conditional_rejection','primary_corollary_and_explanatory_argument_read','Main Theorem 1.1, Conjecture 1.3, Corollary 1.4','Source proves AM membership assuming GRH; combined with Boppana–Hastad–Zachos it concludes not coNP-hard assuming GRH and PH != Pi_2^p. This is an explicit conditional rejection of the authors previous conjecture, not an unconditional disproof.','No campaign claim from a conditional known source consequence. No finite permutation test could establish a complexity-class hardness separation.'),
368077:('parked_asymptotic_frequency_gap','primary_recurrence_and_proofs_plus_extended_prefix','Propositions 3.6 and 3.10; Conjecture 4.2','Derived recurrence sat(k+1)=(3 sat(k)+a)/2 with a=1 for odd sat(k), else a=2. Replicated 525067 ones at k=2^20. At k=2^21 the checkpointed extension gives 1049601 ones and 1047551 twos. Exact extension beyond that range is retained in logs/digit-block*.log. Prefix experiments do not resolve a limiting frequency.','Prove parity balance along the unbounded integer orbit, rather than an observed finite frequency; source warns of Collatz-like difficulty.'),
375523:('parked_source_range_not_extended','primary_auxiliary_definition_and_hook_formula_read_plus_exact_permutations','Auxiliary definition near Theorem 1.4; Theorems 2.5 and 3.5; Conjecture 4.1','Enumerated every rho in S_n for n=1..9 and applied the stack map until zero reaches the front. Exact totals retained in logs/stack.log. The source computes auxiliary means through 37 (bound indexed n=38), so this is a semantic replication, not extended coverage. Its hook formula and growth theorem do not immediately imply convexity of the means.','Need distributional control of t(alpha) beyond width, or a substantially faster exact diagram DP to exceed the source range. No full convexity coupling obtained.'),
375601:('parked_sustained_finite_state_search','primary_conjecture_and_finite_automaton_sections_read_plus_multiple_exact_sweeps','Conjecture 8, Section 4 state/cycle interpretation','Exact DFS cycle detection on task-age vectors tests qualifying sorted instances. Full coverage: 2..6 tasks with periods 2..12; 2..5 tasks with periods 3..20; 2..6 tasks with periods 4..16. Additional partial lexicographic sweeps are logged, with completed-instance counts and last tuple. None refuted the bound.','A counterexample requires an acyclic reachable state graph below the density threshold. A full proof would need a new scheduling decomposition depending on the minimum period; the source 5/6 theorem only resolves the minimum-period 2 and 3 cases.'),
375764:('parked_source_lemma_collapse_outside_hard_case','primary_construction_proof_and_conjecture_plus_exact_automorphisms','Construction 4.1, Remark 4.2, Proposition 4.3, Conjecture 4.5','All 21 positive regular uniform simple labelled input designs on v=2..5 with e in {2,3}, ve <=10 and the conjecture condition were tested for fibre-breaking point automorphisms, using subset incidence counts. None. Source pair-count formulas directly prove the claim for 2-design input when output is not a 2-design; this routine bridge is documented separately and not credited.','Recover the fibre partition in the coincident-pair-count output 2-design case, or for arbitrary 1-design input with overlapping pair counts. Small cases do not settle this.'),
375860:('parked_protected_family_no_duplicate_route','primary_exact_conjecture_and_tables_read','Conjecture 4.5, Table 6','Same alternating-path Ramsey family as protected r112/r110 routes. Source table covers a=3..26,b=3..30. No duplicate SAT or cyclic-to-dihedral reduction attempted. Boundary a,b=2 would be a convention/endpoint check only.','Coordinate ownership before any family-wide proof attempt. This lane has no independent finite-search coverage for this protected family.'),
375861:('parked_protected_family_no_duplicate_route','primary_exact_conjecture_and_tables_read','Conjecture 4.6, Table 7','Same protected family as the preceding record. Source table covers a=3..26,b=3..16. No duplicate search or cyclic-to-dihedral route undertaken.','Coordinate ownership with r112/r110; no independent search coverage claimed.'),
376198:('excluded_source_explicit_refutation','primary_counterexample_and_exact_polynomial_argument_read','Section 5, seven-vertex 18-facet complex and polynomial p(x)','Source gives eigenvalues 7,7,7,alpha1,alpha2 with alpha1+alpha2>12, violating the fifth partial sum 33. The actual facet list, characteristic polynomial, root intervals and dimension-lifting construction are printed. This is not a new counterexample.','None for this campaign route. Huang 2607.20051 is a second prior-art abstract lead, not a separately read proof here.'),
382474:('excluded_source_proved','primary_Sachs_subgraph_proof_and_factorization_read','Theorems 4.1, 4.4 and 4.5; Conjecture 4.6','Source Theorem 4.4 confines Sachs components to the constituent graphs; determinant expansion factors, giving Theorem 4.5 for BAB graphs. The displayed Conjecture 4.6 is expressly verified for R-disjoint graphs.','No new route; no redundant graph sweep.'),
382484:('parked_hard_real_rootedness_gap','primary_exact_conjecture_and_scope_of_new_results_read','Conjecture 1.2 and discussion; Theorems 1.6 and 1.7','Source gamma positivity is weaker than real-rootedness. Its counterexamples for flag chordal nestohedra do not address braid matroids with minimal building sets. No trusted coefficient generator for this exact moduli-space sequence was implemented; no polynomial coverage claimed.','Need the exact sequence recurrence and an exact real-root criterion at large n, or a uniform interlacing theorem. General nestohedral counterexamples cannot be transferred without a semantic bridge.')}
